.Dd November 21, 2026
.Dt JOBMARSHAL 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm jobmarshal
.Nd per-user build coordination service
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm help
.Op Ar command
.Nm
.Cm start
.Op Fl j Ar N | Fl -jobs Ar N
.Nm
.Cm status
.Nm
.Cm stop
.Nm
.Cm version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
manages a private per-user service on Linux and FreeBSD.
The
.Cm help
and
.Cm version
commands print command-line information without accessing service configuration.
.Ss Starting the service
.Cm start
starts a detached daemon with its diagnostics in the private
.Pa daemon.log
file in the runtime directory.
It prints a shell-quoted export of
.Ev JOBMARSHAL_RUNTIME_DIR
on standard output, so a shell can use:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
eval "$(jobmarshal start -j 8)"
.Ed
.Pp
The maximum job capacity comes from
.Fl j
or
.Fl -jobs ,
then
.Ev JOBMARSHAL_JOBS ,
then the number of available CPUs.
The value must be a positive decimal integer.
Starting an existing service succeeds when it is responsive and not draining.
An explicitly requested capacity must match; stop the service before changing it.
.Ss Inspecting and stopping the service
.Cm status
reports the daemon PID, maximum jobs, active and waiting build counts, and draining
state.
The active and waiting counts are currently zero.
.Cm stop
acknowledges the request before teardown and waits for complete shutdown.
Stable lock files remain in the runtime directory after shutdown.
.Ss Runtime directory
The runtime directory is selected from
.Ev JOBMARSHAL_RUNTIME_DIR ,
then the XDG runtime directory with
.Pa jobmarshal
appended, then
.Pa /tmp/jobmarshal- Ns Ar uid
if no usable XDG runtime directory exists.
The final path must be absolute UTF-8 without whitespace.
It must be a real directory owned by the current user without group or other
permissions; a new directory is created with mode 0700.
The service rejects unsafe directories, lock files, and log files.
.Pp
Ordinary control operations have bounded connection and I/O deadlines.
Missing or refused sockets indicate an absent service; other failures are errors.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width JOBMARSHAL_RUNTIME_DIR
.It Ev JOBMARSHAL_RUNTIME_DIR
Explicit private runtime directory.
.It Ev JOBMARSHAL_JOBS
Explicit capacity used when the command line does not select one.
.It Ev XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
XDG runtime base directory, accessed through the XDG library.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
The
.Cm help ,
.Cm start ,
.Cm stop ,
and
.Cm version
commands return 0 on success and 1 on execution failure.
.Cm status
returns 0 when the service responds and 1 when absent or on an error.
Usage errors, including a missing command, return 2.
.Sh SEE ALSO
The project homepage is
.Lk https://github.com/jmmv/jobmarshal .
Report issues at
.Lk https://github.com/jmmv/jobmarshal/issues .
